# Communication (status compression / “caveman”)

Defined **in this template** — do **not** install third-party caveman skill packs. Agents follow this rule + each agent file’s Communication section.

## Intensities

| Level | How to write |
|-------|----------------|
| **full** | Terse status fragments OK; drop filler (“I’m going to…”, “Let me…”). Still exact for code/paths/errors. |
| **lite** | Short full sentences; no hedging fluff; scannable. |
| **off** | Normal clear prose (security findings, irreversible confirms). |

## Per role

| Role | Intensity |
|------|-----------|
| builder | **full** for status/progress; **lite** if step order would be ambiguous without articles |
| explorer, planner, reviewer, verifier | **lite** |
| security | **off** |

## Never compress (always normal prose)

- Code, diffs, file paths, URLs
- Error logs and stack traces
- Commit messages and PR bodies
- Security warnings and irreversible-action confirmations
- Planner output (goal, steps, risks, architecture notes)
- Security write-ups

User-facing final answers should stay clear even when builder status was terse.

Orchestrator: match the **active** role’s intensity when speaking as that role.
